5:[['Unli va undosh tovushlar','O‘zbek tilida 6 ta unli tovush bor: a, o, u, o‘, i, e. Unlilar talaffuzida havo og‘izda to‘siqqa uchramaydi. Qolgan tovushlar undoshlar: b, d, k, s, sh, ch, ng va boshqalar.',[['O‘zbek tilida nechta unli tovush bor?',['5','6','10','29'],1],['Qaysi harf unli tovushni bildiradi?',['b','o‘','sh','q'],1]]],
['Sinonim, antonim, omonim','Sinonimlar — ma’nosi yaqin so‘zlar (chiroyli — go‘zal). Antonimlar — qarama-qarshi ma’noli so‘zlar (katta — kichik). Omonimlar — shakli bir xil, ma’nosi boshqa-boshqa so‘zlar (ot — hayvon, ot — ism).',[['“Issiq” so‘zining antonimi?',['Iliq','Sovuq','Qaynoq','Yoz'],1],['“Do‘st — o‘rtoq” qanday so‘zlar?',['Antonim','Sinonim','Omonim','Paronim'],1]]],
['So‘z tarkibi: o‘zak va qo‘shimcha','O‘zak — so‘zning asosiy ma’nosini bildiruvchi, boshqa qismlarga bo‘linmaydigan qismi. Qo‘shimchalar o‘zakka qo‘shilib, yangi so‘z yasaydi yoki so‘zlarni bog‘laydi. Masalan: paxta-kor-lar-imiz.',[['“Kitobxonlar” so‘zining o‘zagi?',['kitob','xon','lar','kitobxon'],0],['“Ishchi” so‘zidagi “-chi” qanday qo‘shimcha?',['So‘z yasovchi','Ko‘plik','Kelishik','Egalik'],0]]]],
6:[['Ot','Ot — shaxs, narsa yoki voqea nomini bildiruvchi so‘z turkumi, kim? nima? qayer? so‘roqlariga javob beradi. Otlar atoqli (Toshkent, Malika) va turdosh (shahar, qiz) bo‘ladi. Atoqli otlar bosh harf bilan yoziladi.',[['Qaysi so‘z atoqli ot?',['daryo','Amudaryo','kitob','maktab'],1],['Ot qaysi so‘roqqa javob beradi?',['Qanday?','Nima?','Qancha?','Nima qildi?'],1]]],
['Sifat va uning darajalari','Sifat predmetning belgisini bildiradi va qanday? qanaqa? so‘roqlariga javob beradi. Sifat darajalari: oddiy (baland), qiyosiy (balandroq), orttirma (eng baland, juda baland).',[['“Shirinroq” sifatning qaysi darajasida?',['Oddiy','Qiyosiy','Orttirma','Hech qaysi'],1],['Sifat qaysi so‘roqqa javob beradi?',['Kim?','Qanday?','Nima qildi?','Qachon?'],1]]],
['Son','Son predmetning miqdori yoki tartibini bildiradi: nechta? qancha? nechanchi? Miqdor son: besh, o‘n. Tartib son -(i)nchi qo‘shimchasi bilan yasaladi: beshinchi, o‘ninchi.',[['Qaysi so‘z tartib son?',['yetti','yettinchi','yettita','yettov'],1],['Tartib son qaysi qo‘shimcha bilan yasaladi?',['-ta','-(i)nchi','-lab','-roq'],1]]]],
7:[['Fe’l va uning zamonlari','Fe’l harakat yoki holatni bildiradi: nima qildi? nima qilyapti? nima qiladi? Fe’l uch zamonda keladi: o‘tgan (o‘qidi), hozirgi (o‘qiyapti), kelasi (o‘qiydi).',[['“Yozyapti” qaysi zamonda?',['O‘tgan','Hozirgi','Kelasi','Hech qaysi'],1],['Qaysi so‘z fe’l?',['chiroyli','yugurdi','daraxt','tez'],1]]],
['Ravish','Ravish harakatning belgisini bildiradi: qanday? qachon? qayerda? qancha? Masalan: tez yurdi, ertaga keladi, oldinga qaradi. Ravish asosan fe’lga bog‘lanadi.',[['“U sekin gapirdi” gapida ravish qaysi?',['U','sekin','gapirdi','Hammasi'],1],['Ravish asosan qaysi so‘z turkumiga bog‘lanadi?',['Otga','Fe’lga','Songa','Olmoshga'],1]]],
['Yordamchi so‘zlar','Ko‘makchilar (uchun, bilan, kabi), bog‘lovchilar (va, lekin, ammo, yoki) va yuklamalar (-mi, faqat, hatto) mustaqil ma’noga ega emas. Ular so‘z va gaplarni bog‘lash yoki qo‘shimcha ma’no berish uchun xizmat qiladi.',[['“Lekin” qaysi yordamchi so‘z turiga kiradi?',['Ko‘makchi','Bog‘lovchi','Yuklama','Undov'],1],['“Vatan uchun” birikmasidagi “uchun” — …',['Ko‘makchi','Bog‘lovchi','Fe’l','Sifat'],0]]]],
8:[['So‘z birikmasi','So‘z birikmasi — kamida ikki mustaqil so‘zning ma’no va grammatik jihatdan bog‘lanishi. Unda hokim va tobe so‘z bo‘ladi: “qizil olma” birikmasida “olma” — hokim, “qizil” — tobe so‘z.',[['“Yangi kitob” birikmasida hokim so‘z?',['yangi','kitob','ikkalasi','hech biri'],1],['Qaysi biri so‘z birikmasi?',['va','maktab hovlisi','-lar','juda'],1]]],
['Ega va kesim','Ega — gapda kim? nima? so‘rog‘iga javob beruvchi bosh bo‘lak. Kesim — eganing harakati yoki belgisini bildiradi: nima qildi? qanday? Masalan: “Quyosh chiqdi” — quyosh (ega), chiqdi (kesim).',[['“Bolalar o‘ynashyapti” gapida ega?',['Bolalar','o‘ynashyapti','ikkalasi','yo‘q'],0],['Kesim nimani bildiradi?',['Eganing harakati yoki belgisini','Faqat joyni','Faqat vaqtni','Undovni'],0]]],
['Ikkinchi darajali bo‘laklar','To‘ldiruvchi (kimni? nimaga?), aniqlovchi (qanday? kimning?) va hol (qachon? qayerda? qanday?) — gapning ikkinchi darajali bo‘laklari. “Aziz kecha qiziqarli kitob o‘qidi” gapida: kecha — hol, qiziqarli — aniqlovchi, kitob — to‘ldiruvchi.',[['Hol qaysi so‘roqqa javob beradi?',['Kimni?','Qachon?','Kimning?','Kim?'],1],['“Chiroyli gul” birikmasida “chiroyli” qaysi bo‘lak?',['Aniqlovchi','To‘ldiruvchi','Hol','Ega'],0]]]],
9:[['Bog‘langan qo‘shma gap','Ikki yoki undan ortiq sodda gap teng huquqli bo‘lib, bog‘lovchilar (va, ammo, lekin, yoki) yoki ohang orqali bog‘lanadi. Masalan: “Yomg‘ir to‘xtadi, quyosh chiqdi.”',[['Bog‘langan qo‘shma gapni toping:',['Men kitob o‘qidim.','Qor yog‘di, lekin havo iliq edi.','Agar kelsang, boramiz.','Ukam maktabga bordi.'],1],['Bog‘langan qo‘shma gap qismlari qanday munosabatda?',['Teng','Biri hokim, biri tobe','Faqat so‘roq','Bog‘lanmagan'],0]]],
['Ergashgan qo‘shma gap','Bir gap (ergash gap) ikkinchisiga (bosh gapga) tobe bo‘ladi. Ular -sa, -ki, chunki, agar kabi vositalar bilan bog‘lanadi: “Agar harakat qilsang, maqsadingga erishasan.”',[['“Agar … -sa” vositasi qaysi gapda ishlatiladi?',['Ergashgan qo‘shma gap','Sodda gap','Bog‘langan qo‘shma gap','Undov gap'],0],['Ergashgan qo‘shma gapda tobe qism nima deyiladi?',['Bosh gap','Ergash gap','Kesim','Undalma'],1]]],
['Nutq uslublari','O‘zbek tilida beshta asosiy uslub bor: so‘zlashuv, ilmiy, rasmiy, publitsistik va badiiy. Masalan, ariza rasmiy uslubda, she’r badiiy uslubda, gazeta maqolasi publitsistik uslubda yoziladi.',[['Ariza qaysi uslubda yoziladi?',['Badiiy','Rasmiy','So‘zlashuv','Publitsistik'],1],['Gazeta maqolasi odatda qaysi uslubda?',['Publitsistik','Ilmiy','Badiiy','So‘zlashuv'],0]]]]
},
eng:{
5:[['To be: am / is / are','“To be” fe’li hozirgi zamonda uch shaklda: I am; he / she / it is; we / you / they are. Misol: I am a pupil. She is my sister. They are friends.',[['My brother ___ 12 years old.',['am','is','are','be'],1],['We ___ in the 5th grade.',['is','am','are','be'],2]]],
['Plural nouns','Ko‘plik odatda -s qo‘shib yasaladi: book → books. s, sh, ch, x bilan tugasa -es: box → boxes. Ba’zi so‘zlar alohida shaklga ega: child → children, man → men, foot → feet.',[['Plural of “box”?',['boxs','boxes','boxies','box'],1],['Plural of “child”?',['childs','childes','children','childen'],2]]],
['Have got / has got','Egalikni bildiradi: I / you / we / they have got; he / she / it has got. Misol: I have got a cat. She has got two brothers. Inkor: haven’t got / hasn’t got.',[['She ___ a new bike.',['have got','has got','is got','are got'],1],['They ___ a big house.',['has got','have got','is','am'],1]]]],
6:[['Present Simple','Odatiy, takrorlanadigan ishlar uchun. He / she / it bilan fe’lga -s qo‘shiladi: She plays tennis every day. So‘roq va inkorda do / does: Does he like music? I don’t like milk.',[['He ___ to school every day.',['go','goes','going','gone'],1],['___ you like pizza?',['Does','Do','Is','Are'],1]]],
['Present Continuous','Ayni paytda bo‘layotgan ish: am / is / are + fe’l-ing. Misol: I am reading now. They are playing football. Signal so‘zlar: now, at the moment, Look!',[['Look! The children ___ in the park.',['play','plays','are playing','played'],2],['She ___ a book now.',['reads','is reading','read','are reading'],1]]],
['Can / can’t','Qobiliyat yoki imkoniyatni bildiradi, barcha shaxslar bilan bir xil: I can swim. He can’t drive. Can you speak English? — Yes, I can.',[['Fish ___ swim.',['can','cans','can to','is can'],0],['Correct question?',['Can she sing?','Does she can sing?','She can sing?','Cans she sing?'],0]]]],
7:[['Past Simple','O‘tgan zamonda tugagan ish. To‘g‘ri fe’llarga -ed qo‘shiladi (play → played), noto‘g‘ri fe’llar alohida yodlanadi (go → went, see → saw). So‘roq va inkorda did: Did you watch it? I didn’t go.',[['Past form of “go”?',['goed','went','gone','goes'],1],['Yesterday I ___ football.',['play','played','playing','plays'],1]]],
['Comparatives and superlatives','Qisqa sifatlar: tall → taller → the tallest. Uzun sifatlar: beautiful → more beautiful → the most beautiful. Istisnolar: good → better → the best; bad → worse → the worst.',[['An elephant is ___ than a dog.',['big','bigger','biggest','more big'],1],['This is ___ day of my life!',['the best','the goodest','better','best'],0]]],
['There is / there are, some / any','Biror narsa mavjudligini bildiradi: There is a pen on the desk. There are some apples. So‘roq va inkorda odatda any: Are there any eggs? There aren’t any chairs.',[['There ___ three cats in the garden.',['is','are','be','am'],1],['Is there ___ milk in the fridge?',['some','any','a','many'],1]]]],
8:[['Present Perfect','have / has + fe’lning 3-shakli (V3). O‘tmishda bo‘lib, natijasi hozir muhim bo‘lgan ish: I have finished my homework. She has never been to London. Signal so‘zlar: already, yet, ever, never, just.',[['I ___ already ___ my lunch.',['have / eaten','has / eaten','have / ate','am / eating'],0],['She ___ never been to Paris.',['have','has','is','did'],1]]],
['Future: will va be going to','Will — to‘satdan qaror va bashorat: I think it will rain. Be going to — oldindan rejalashtirilgan ish: I am going to visit my grandma tomorrow.',[['Reja: We ___ travel to Samarkand next week.',['are going to','will be','goes','went'],0],['I think she ___ win.',['will','is','going','did'],0]]],
['Modal verbs: must, should','Must — majburiyat: You must wear a seatbelt. Mustn’t — qat’iy taqiq. Should — maslahat: You should drink more water. Modal fe’ldan keyin fe’l “to”siz keladi.',[['You ___ eat so much sugar. It’s bad for you.',['should','shouldn’t','must to','can to'],1],['Students ___ be quiet in the library.',['must','musts','must to','musted'],0]]]],
9:[['Passive voice','Ishni kim bajargani emas, ishning o‘zi muhim bo‘lganda: be + V3. Present: English is spoken in many countries. Past: The book was written in 1990.',[['This house ___ in 1950.',['built','was built','is build','was build'],1],['Football ___ all over the world.',['is played','plays','is playing','played'],0]]],
['Conditionals: 1st va 2nd','First conditional — real shart: If it rains, I will stay at home. Second conditional — xayoliy shart: If I had a million dollars, I would travel the world.',[['If I ___ time, I will help you.',['have','had','will have','would have'],0],['If I were a bird, I ___ fly.',['will','would','am','can to'],1]]],
['Reported speech','Birovning gapini o‘zlashtirib aytish. Zamon bir pog‘ona orqaga suriladi: “I am tired,” he said. → He said (that) he was tired. Olmoshlar ham o‘zgaradi: my → his / her.',[['“I like tea,” she said. → She said she ___ tea.',['like','liked','likes','is liking'],1],['“I can swim,” Tom said. → Tom said he ___ swim.',['can','could','cans','will'],1]]]]
},
